## Count appearance of values

To count how many times each clothing category appears in the dataframe above, you can use `value_counts` in Polars. Here's how to do it:

::: {#c31e681c .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 ['category']
 .value_counts(sort=True)
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (3, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>category</th><th>count</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>u32</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Sweater&quot;</td><td>526</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Socks&quot;</td><td>297</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Hat&quot;</td><td>177</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


## Doing it the idiomatic way

If you want to impress your colleagues with your Polars knowledge, you can do it the idiomatic way (which I highly encourage).

::: {#1e192ece .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .select('category')
 .to_series()
 .value_counts(sort=True)
 )
```

